From 6fc70be17e8e5502f78daa0e62f5dfe5ef8410d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick <nekreshen@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:37:40 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] gpu: gpu_vblank_display_sync, the guest vblank on the
 display's refreshes

The guest vblank timed by its own clock drifts against the display's:
frames cross refresh boundaries, so some refreshes show two new frames
(one never seen) or none, and at a higher rate the newest frame at each
refresh advances the picture unevenly. With gpu_vblank_display_sync
(macOS, off by default) a CoreVideo display link fires one vblank per
refresh of the display, so a game that keeps up shows one new frame per
refresh. FIFA 19 in a match on a 60 Hz display: 60.0 frames shown a
second, none repeated or dropped, each advancing 16.66 +- 0.37 ms (at
its own 240 Hz clock: 12-24 ms). Without a refresh for 2.5 periods (the
display asleep) a vblank fires anyway.
